Description: digiKam's Enable 3D is the stereo layer's; a 3D choice that cannot follow a moved file is told (ORDER 551c)
 The program's lasting switch that shows every picture flat is the layer's Stereo::Enable3DAction, the same words in every
 program on the layer, in place of a second Not 3D; Alt+Shift+N switches it and the slide show starts with it too. A
 stored 3D choice that cannot follow a file digiKam itself renamed or moved is told to the person from the main thread,
 one window for a burst; a folder moved to another device by a copy carries its files' choices. Needs
 libstereo-layer-dev (>= 1.19.2).
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-15
